			OSQL
	      ORACLE Visual SQL Query Tool

---------------------------------------------------------------
		       Menu Bar
---------------------------------------------------------------

The following menu buttons and associated menu items are
available on the menu bar:

%%hyperhelp_mark File%%
----------
  File
----------

  Load SQL...		Load a file into the SQL statement
			text entry area using a file selector
			widget.

  Save			Save the text in the SQL statement text
  			entry area in to the current save file
  			as indicated.
			
  Save SQL As...		Save into a file the text in the SQL
  			statement text entry area using a file
  			selector widget.

  Clear SQL Stmt Buffer	Clear all statements in the current
  			SQL query buffer.
			
  New Connection...	Terminate this connection and login
  			again with a new userid and password.

  Exit			Logout of ORACLE and exit osql.


%%hyperhelp_mark Props%%
----------
  Props
----------

  Print...			Edit the command used to print output.
  			The default is "lpr".

  Results Query Window	Set toggle to either "Show" or "Hide" the SQL
  			statement that created the results displayed
  			in the Results Window.  The default is to 
  			"Hide" the SQL.


%%hyperhelp_mark Options%%
----------
  DB Options
----------

  Autocommit		Turn autocommit mode "on" or "off".
  			Osql defaults to autocommit on.

  Commit Now		Commit all transactions executed since
  			last commit.

  Rollback Now		Rollback outstanding transactions.

  SQL Trace		Turn SQL trace facility on or off.

  Execute PL/SQL...	Start a %%
  hyperhelp_link "tool" Osql.plsql%% to execute PL/SQL code.
  
  
%%hyperhelp_mark Objects%%
----------
  Objects
----------

  Describe Table...	Describe a particular table owned by 
  			a specific owner.  If no owner information 
  			is entered, a list of all tables matching 
  			the requested name will be returned.

  Tables			List all of the tables in this ORACLE
  			instance.

  Views			List all of the views in this ORACLE
			instance.

  Indexes		List all of the indexes in this ORACLE
			instance.


  Procedures		List all of the procedures in this
			ORACLE instance.


  Triggers		List all of the triggers in this ORACLE
			instance.

%%hyperhelp_mark Help%%
----------
  Help
----------

  Version...		Display current program information.

  Application...		Display help on how to use osql.
  